{
  "inquiry": "Hello,\nWe want ONE prototype of a custom trail overshirt, using a new pattern rather than enlarging an existing style. Our material targets are 12K waterproofness and 8K breathability. We have attached shape-notes.pdf with our fit direction. Please tell us how you would start, the prototype cost and normal development time, and whether you can ship the prototype to Finland. Bulk production would be considered only after prototype approval.\nThank you.",
  "lightweight_business_brief": {
    "aim": "Prepare a minimum sufficient first reply for human approval.",
    "operator_focus": "Begin assessing the written specifications now; review the existing shape-notes before making fit assumptions or asking for information they may contain. Verify available material options and relevant test evidence with suppliers. Conditional prototype costing can proceed in parallel, dependent on the route; no firm prototype price is currently authorized. Answer the normal 18-business-day development reference with fee/material conditions and authorized Finland shipment. One prototype is already known: never ask sample quantity or request the already-referenced file again. If useful, ask the expected first production quantity after prototype approval, expressly without making it a prerequisite to current prototype assessment. The 12K/8K figures stay customer targets, and bulk interest stays conditional interest.",
